  "unscored": [
    "tapped glyph opened or listed in 100% of taps (tap fixture, every interactive glyph centre in whole chart, Leponnia z3.5, Epēshu z4.55, Epēshu z4.95, city z6.15, on iphone13 and pixel7)",
    "chooser shown iff >= 2 glyph centres lie within 22 px (scripted on the 10 most crowded pairs); rows >= 44 px, nearest first, names plus kind. Central ruling 2026-10-07: a tap with no glyph centre within 22 px opens no MARKER card (pads never decide); on a VISIBLE line, fill or printed place label it does what it did before (that feature own card), and on a faded (invisible) line or fill it opens nothing. The chooser closes on any tap outside it and never stays over a card",
    "faded (tier-hidden) markers take no input on any profile: elementsFromPoint at a faded marker glyph centre returns no faded marker. On coarse pointers faded lines and fills (realm, district, way, lane, route and trail panes) take no tap either, so elementsFromPoint there returns no faded element at all; on fine pointers faded lines and fills keep their hover and click exactly as before (desktop identity). Desktop sequential focus skips faded markers (declared, not a finding)",
    "glyphs never move (no badge offset): marker glyph rects equal R1; desktop click fixture opens the same hashes as R1 (except clicks that landed on faded waypoints, which now reach the marker beneath: listed as the declared change)",
    "if A-U2 is deferred-5b the unit proceeds against B0 tiers and records tiers_deferred:true",
    "desktop chrome controls are unchanged (bullet 8); the desktop card view is unchanged (bullet 9)",
    "the chooser sheet clears the home bar with its own env(safe-area-inset-*) padding; the unit uses exactly the fixed chooser words, voice read by the lens"
